WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.374
My keyboard has become a decoration.

00:00:03.374 --> 00:00:10.319
Recently, I've been using voice input and AI together, to replace my keyboard.

00:00:10.319 --> 00:00:16.302
In the last few months, I've dictated more than 130,000 English words,

00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:18.253
and that's outside of work.

00:00:18.253 --> 00:00:22.463
If you count all of the words I typed in using voice control,

00:00:22.463 --> 00:00:25.408
that's probably twice as much as that.

00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:31.110
AI being able to comprehend, understand what you mean exactly,

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.816
there is no need to type precisely.

00:00:33.816 --> 00:00:41.148
You can basically use voice control to tell the rough ideas, the rough meaning, to AI,

00:00:41.148 --> 00:00:45.901
and they can format the ideas in the perfect sense.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.625
Let's take a real example.

00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:50.908
This morning, I need to reply a Slack message.

00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:57.244
Probably a few hundred words. In the past, it's going to take 15 to 20 minutes to reply.

00:00:57.244 --> 00:01:02.700
But instead, I say these sentences to AI, via voice control:

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:10.266
'Help me reply to these Slack messages. Don't send anything. Just draft the message.

00:01:10.266 --> 00:01:12.890
There are three things I want to deliver to the person.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:17.260
First thing is, I agree that this is a true customer experience problem

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:20.062
that we need to prioritize to fix immediately.

00:01:20.062 --> 00:01:26.578
The second thing is, I don't think we need a full analysis before we start fixing anything,

00:01:26.578 --> 00:01:32.162
because out of these many problems, there are a few low-hanging fruit there

00:01:32.162 --> 00:01:35.483
that we can pretty much start fixing straight away.

00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:42.268
The third thing is, we should involve Bob Smith from the other team into this area,

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:47.847
because he has done recent analysis in this area.'

00:01:47.847 --> 00:01:52.938
And that's it. 20 seconds later, there is a very well formatted message,

00:01:52.938 --> 00:01:57.153
full of context, a lot of information pulled from previous conversations

00:01:57.153 --> 00:02:02.707
injected into the message, delivered in three points, to my colleague.

00:02:02.707 --> 00:02:08.126
So this is my two cents of how to use AI to increase your productivity,

00:02:08.126 --> 00:02:11.655
to manage better in the age of AI.
